hamango/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## MAINTAINER-AGENT-0001 — Phase 0\n\nCloses no issue; establishes the contract scaffold for #509.\n\n### Included\n\n- provider-neutral immutable PR snapshot, audit receipt, risk classes, and merge observation model;\n- pure merge-authority evaluator with SHA/base/policy binding;\n- pairwise author/auditor/broker identity separation;\n- permanent R3 constitutional firewall;\n- explicit state machine with no shortcut to MERGED;\n- separate audit, policy, and merge-finality JSON schemas;\n- disabled-by-default pilot policy for this repository;\n- architecture and staged rollout;\n- nine dependency-free contract tests.\n\n### Verified\n\n`python -m unittest -v tests.test_maintainer_agent_contract`\n\nResult: 9 tests passed.\n\nJSON files parse successfully and Python modules compile.\n\n### Safety boundary\n\nThis draft contains no webhook activation, credentials, GitHub App installation, ruleset mutation, production service, or merge authority. The pilot policy is `enabled: false`. Changes under `maintainer_agent/**` are themselves R3 and cannot be auto-merged by the proposed system.\n\n### Independent review questions\n\n1. Is pairwise identity separation sufficient for the first shadow deployment?\n2. Should base SHA drift always invalidate PASS, or may a policy allow proof-preserving rebases?\n3. Which historical 30 PRs should seed the false-PASS/false-block corpus?\n4. Where should the append-only receipt store live for GitHub + Forgejo portability?\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-08T04:38:10Z","updated_at":"2026-10-08T04:38:10Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"2ff995dcc1aa9a45fbdee3f33ed128c9a2b22826","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"pashamango:project/maintainer-agent-0001","ref":"project/maintainer-agent-0001","repo":{"id":1257706201,"node_